<header><p class="enc-kicker">Event</p><h1 class="enc-title">Flight to Varennes</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1791">1791</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/18th-century">18th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Flight to Varennes was the attempted escape of King <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/louis-xvi">Louis XVI</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/marie-antoinette">Marie Antoinette</a> and their children from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/paris">Paris</a> on the night of 20–21 June 1791. Hoping to reach royalist troops near the eastern frontier, they were recognised and stopped at Varennes-en-Argonne and brought back to Paris. The episode destroyed public trust in the king and strengthened republican feeling in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/french-revolution">French Revolution</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/flight-to-varennes.jpg" alt="Flight to Varennes" width="320" height="232" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Thomas Falcon Marshall · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Arrest_of_Louis_XVI_and_his_Family,_Varennes,_1791.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
